**Read:** [Petrology — Stephen A. Nelson, Tulane EENS 2120](../sources/Petrology-Nelson-Tulane.lingua#r_1MNEKH4WW2GQRD4FZWNRD1GDPZ), the complete magma-differentiation, mixing, and assimilation notes; [Advanced Igneous Petrology — Timothy Grove, MIT 12.490](../sources/MIT-Advanced-Igneous-Petrology.lingua#r_3R0PJP97ZPE1RSGPPGY8WXXQZF), the full selected case with its original papers; [General chemistry](../../../../hephaestus/chemistry/general-chemistry/General-chemistry.lingua#r_206GS6CVXD8WSY1VX7PRF7136V), material/energy balances and mixture definitions as needed.

Mixing combines material from identified endmembers; assimilation incorporates surrounding or introduced material through a process with thermal/chemical consequences. A linear two-endmember mass balance is useful only when quantities, basis, endmembers, and conserved components are specified.

For invented concentrations 10 and 50 units on one mass basis, a mixture with 25 percent of the second endmember has concentration 20. Ratios and isotopic ratios generally do not mix by averaging their ratio values with the same simple weights; denominators and constituent inventories matter.

Assimilation can involve partial melting, reaction, crystallization, heat transfer, and evolving endmembers. A chemical fit may require an energetically or physically implausible amount of material. Mineral populations, resorption, inclusions, spatial relationships, and chronological evidence can test a purely compositional interpretation.

**Work:** derive/check a two-component mass account and show an example where ratio averaging fails. Compare fractional crystallization, mixing, and assimilation as explanations for a documented trend using complete original case papers. Add a bounded heat/energy constraint and explain which physical assumptions control it. Identify a mineral/domain observation that discriminates the alternatives.

Read the full mixing/assimilation notes and advanced case material. Preserve endmember uncertainty and avoid selecting endmembers only because they make the observed line fit. The storage sequence develops how multiple populations and processes can be assembled into one final rock.

